  "stamp.heading": "Your blueprints, all in one place.",
  "stamp.description117": "All stamps from your current in-game library. Organised by region and game folder, with scale floor plans and downloadable PNGs.",
  "stamp.description1800": "Floor plans with buildings, field modules, roads and railways. Organised by game region and stamp folder.",
  "map.description": "The gallery groups local saves by seed and saved map configuration. Click a map to open the full-size PNG.",
  "map.notes": "Notes on maps and playtime",
  "map.totalNote": "Total playtime uses the highest saved playtime for each game.",
  "map.geometry117": "The maps combine saved island positions and rotations with graphics from the local game installation. They show islands and terrain, without cities, buildings or ownership. In Aegyptus, seams may be visible between the province's four terrain sections.",
  "map.geometry1800": "The maps combine saved island positions and rotations with graphics from the local game installation. They show islands and terrain, without cities, buildings or ownership. A ring marks islands without matching graphics. Regions missing from the selected save are not shown.",
  "map.geometry1404": "Maps are reconstructed directly from the saved terrain. They show islands and terrain, without cities, buildings or ownership.",
  "map.time117": "Timestamps come from the saves and use the configured time zone. Playtime uses the saved active-time counter when available; older saves may only contain the game-time counter. Recognised settings display their names; unknown values retain the stored value. World and island sizes come from the generated regions where available.",
  "map.time1800": "Timestamps come from the saves and use the configured time zone. Ties in highest playtime use the newest save. File counts include autosaves and archived copies. Scenarios and campaigns can store a seed even when parts of their maps are predefined. IDs are the stored values. Island counts, sizes and active DLCs refer to the selected save.",
  "map.time1404": "Dates use file modification timestamps in the computer's local time zone. Playtime comes from saved game statistics. Identical save copies are grouped; the summary lists additional copies separately.",
