  "stamp.lavenderIntro": "For",
  "stamp.lavenderNote": "yellow hatched areas mark expansion tiles left free compared with the Ceres version. Click a blueprint to open the enlarged view, then click the image to see its original size. Ceres is identified from saved field areas and their base requirements; the indicator applies to complete fields, not building unlocks. Cosmetic DLC indicators refer to included decorations. Uncertain assignments are marked separately. This is a schematic view, not an in-game image.",
  "stamp.techNote": "Blueprints use saved positions and installed building footprints. DLC requirements are inferred from included objects and identifiable skins. Optional unused skins do not count. Unknown footprints and skins are marked. Town halls and trade unions show their counts. Tractors and silos are detected as included modules. Electricity distinguishes required operation, possible production bonuses and existing power plants. Connections, ranges, fuel, feed and production ratios are not simulated; items can change the base values.",
